%N A100746 Inverse modulo 2 binomial transform of Jacobsthal numbers J(n).
%C A100746 J(n) may be retrieved as Sum_{k=0..n} (binomial(n,k) mod 2)*a(k).
%H A100746 Andrew Howroyd, <a href="/A100746/b100746.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%F A100746 a(n) = Sum_{k=0..n} (-1)^A010060(n-k)*(binomial(n, k) mod 2)*A001045(k).
%o A100746 (PARI) a(n) = sum(k=0, n, (-1)^(hammingweight(n-k))*(binomial(n,k) % 2)*(2^k - (-1)^k)/3) \\ _Andrew Howroyd_, Aug 08 2026
%Y A100746 Cf. A001045, A010060.
%K A100746 easy,nonn
